    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a1">

                <pb facs="0314" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1048"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 293.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Mr. Elmore.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1891-08-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 19, 1891</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 51.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I would respectfully call your
                    excellency’s attention to the notes from this legation, No. 2, of November 5,
                    1889; No. 27, of October 16, 1890, and No. 41, of July 16, 1891, in reference to
                    the claim of the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, and kindly ask if your
                    excellency will have this claim presented to the present Congress for its early
                    attention.</p>
                <p>Expressing the hope that some action will be taken in this long-pending claim, I
                    beg to renew to your excellency the assurance of my consideration and
                    esteem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
